---
const vectors = [
  {
    title: "Hallucination",
    body:
      "An LLM decides on its own to transfer the entire balance to a fabricated address.",
  },
  {
    title: "Prompt injection",
    body:
      "Hostile input manipulates the agent into signing a malicious transaction.",
  },
  {
    title: "Intent drift",
    body:
      "The agent says 'pay $0.01 for API X' but the actual TX sends 5 SOL somewhere else.",
  },
];
---

<section aria-labelledby="problem-heading">
  <h2 id="problem-heading">The problem</h2>
  <p>
    AI agents are already transacting autonomously on Solana via the x402
    standard. Giving them direct custody of private keys creates three attack
    vectors with no standard defense:
  </p>
  <div class="grid">
    {vectors.map((v) => (
      <article class="card">
        <h3>{v.title}</h3>
        <p>{v.body}</p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>
